    "created_at": "2018-01-10T00:33:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-10T00:33:25Z",
    "body": "XHR onabort is just at the top of my list because in chromium's implementation, an XHR onabort handler is a particularly effective way to queue a fetch very late in the document discard process. I'm not sure if this is the spec's intention, but in chromium, no matter how late in the process an XHR gets aborted, we fire onabort.\r\n\r\nIdeally, after a certain point in the document unload process, we can guarantee fetch-related event handlers like onabort won't run anymore. My naive thought is that, after that point, requests are ignored unless they're explicitly of a type permitted to outlive the Document (e.g., fetch keepalive) or that intentionally omits response handling (e.g., sendBeacon).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
