    "created_at": "2018-01-10T11:21:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-10T11:21:59Z",
    "body": "I mean that from an \"XHR onabort\" you can also create fetches through other means than using `XMLHttpRequest` again. It seems reasonable that once `unload` is dispatched we set a flag and Fetch basically prevents all outgoing traffic (except for keepalive; which hopefully includes sendBeacon once refactored). That still leaves WebRTC which would have to be independently patched. But I'm not sure if that's what you were aiming for?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
